You are helping me build an event-driven order and inventory pipeline as a
learning project. My goal is to UNDERSTAND the infrastructure, not just ship it.

Hard rules:
- Build in thin vertical slices. One service end to end before starting the next.
  Never scaffold all infrastructure at once.
- Before generating any Terraform resource or container config, explain in plain
  language: what it is, why it's needed here, and what breaks if we remove it.
- After generating Terraform, walk me through what `terraform plan` will show
  before I apply. Never auto-apply.
- When I ask "why," give the real tradeoff, not a generic answer. Name the
  alternative I'm not choosing and why.
- Treat all generated code as a draft I will interrogate, not a final answer.
- Keep a DECISIONS.md log. After each meaningful choice, append a short entry:
  what we chose, what we rejected, and why.
- No secrets in code, .tf files, or state. Use Secrets Manager / SSM from the start.
- Stop and ask me before moving to the next phase.
